# ==============================================================================
# Git Ignore Configuration
# Project: PAJ2 (Modern Vanilla HTML5 / CSS3 / ES6+)
# ==============================================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# STEP 1: Sensitive Information, Credentials & Environment Secrets
# Why: Prevents private API keys, environment configs, and cryptographic keys
# from ever leaking into remote version control repositories.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.production
.env.development
.env.local
.env.*.local
*.env
*.key
*.pem
*.cert
*.crt
*.pfx
*.p12
credentials.json
id_rsa
id_rsa.pub

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# STEP 2: Package Dependencies & Package Manager Locks
# Why: Dependencies can be re-installed deterministically; committing them bloats
# repository size and causes merge conflicts.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
jspm_packages/
web_modules/
vendor/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# STEP 3: Build Outputs, Bundlers & Temporary Caches
# Why: Generated assets and caches belong to the local build environment,
# not version control.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
dist/
build/
out/
.cache/
.parcel-cache/
.turbo/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# STEP 4: Logs, Diagnostics & Runtime Traces
# Why: Ephemeral logs created during local dev or package installations.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
logs/
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# STEP 5: IDEs, Editors & Developer Workspace Settings
# Why: Developer-specific configurations should not overwrite teammates' environments.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?
*.sublime-workspace
*.sublime-project

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# STEP 6: Operating System Artifacts & Metadata
# Why: System-generated hidden files created by Windows File Explorer, macOS Finder, etc.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Windows
Thumbs.db
Thumbs.db:encryptable
ehthumbs.db
ehthumbs_vista.db
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# macOS
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
._*

# Linux / General temp
*~
*.bak
*.tmp
*.temp

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# STEP 7: Testing & Code Coverage Reports
# Why: Test execution outputs and coverage metrics change on every test run.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
coverage/
.nyc_output/

# TODO: If automated visual regression testing or Lighthouse CI runs are introduced,
# verify and append `.lighthouseci/` or visual diff artifact folders here.
